!!!!!!!!!!!!!!  Polarisation e2e deck: elliptical, averaged  !!!!!!!!!!!!!!
!!
!!  One of five small 1D decks run by testMPIIntegrationPolarisation.pf.
!!  The other 1D goldens are a 'puffin' (1, 1) undulator with no ends
!!  (f1main) and plane-pole with ends (osc_taper), and none ran averaged
!!  mode; these add the 'helical' and elliptical field branches, their
!!  entry and exit ramps, and the averaged solver.
!!
!!  Built on f1main: the same cold, noise-free beam (inputs/beam_file.in,
!!  319 macroparticles, no RNG), rho = 0.01, gamma_r = 100, aw = 1. Six
!!  periods with undulator ends - two of ramp in, two of main section, two
!!  of ramp out - and a seed, so the beam and field both move: zbar = 0.75,
!!  0.75 gain lengths, the power moving by 1-2%, far from saturation.
!!
!!  Averaged mode (qAveraged) at sux = 0.5, suy = 1: the two Cartesian
!!  envelopes are driven with different couplings and Bessel factors.
!!
!!  Goldens: see the regeneration note in testMPIIntegrationPolarisation.pf.
!!
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

&MDATA
 qOneD                  = .true.
 beam_file              = 'inputs/beam_file.in'
 seed_file              = 'inputs/1D/pol_seed_circ.in'
 q_noise                = .false.
 qUndEnds               = .true.
 sElectronThreshold     = 0.05
 nodesPerLambdar        = 17
 sFModelLengthZ2        = 4.0
 srho                   = 0.01
 sux                    = 0.5
 suy                    = 1.0
 saw                    = 1.0
 sgamma_r               = 100.0
 lambda_w               = 0.04
 zundType               = ''
 taper                  = 0.0
 lattFile               = ''
 stepsPerPeriod         = 4
 nPeriods               = 6
 iWriteNthSteps         = 100000
 iWriteIntNthSteps      = 100000
 qAveraged              = .true.
 lambdarPerCell         = 1.0
 /
